{"type":"message","id":"5e044a20","parentId":"253a21ba","timestamp":"2026-05-21T11:25:01.186Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_zhc2kzl2dHBOoBUASFyx27bg","toolName":"memory_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5032607a95dc79a1db6f6cebad75e040ac84ca717b59ceede51aabb3ced8c113\",\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 1112,\n      \"endLine\": 1189,\n      \"score\": 1,\n      \"textScore\": 0.5718379351392922,\n      \"snippet\": \"No idle pause before WordPress confirmation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Test B — Approval required during article step\\n- article exec requires approval\\n\\n### Pass condition\\n- pipeline pauses only for approval\\n- after approval, it resumes automatically from article step\\n- does not restart earlier steps\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Test C — Research fails once\\n- invalid JSON first time\\n- valid second time\\n\\n### Pass condition\\n- auto retry happens\\n- pipeline continues automatically\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Test D — Chart fails twice\\n- chart invalid twice\\n\\n### Pass condition\\n- pipeline continues without chart\\n- no raw broken placeholder leaks into final export path\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Test E — Image generation fails\\n### Pass condition\\n- pipeline continues to Dr\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L1112-L1189\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"citation\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L1112-L1189\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cf5a8f124099a149c88763e41ecc67fee3917add3afd4c60ed202ac4c339a4b0\",\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 557,\n      \"endLine\": 633,\n      \"score\": 1,\n      \"textScore\": 0.49100387456715194,\n      \"snippet\": \"- if `user_input_required=true`, then `status` must be `awaiting_user_confirmation`\\n- if `approval_required=true`, then `status` must be `blocked_approval`\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 5) Orchestration rules\\n\\n## 5.1 Step completion rule\\nWhen a step finishes successfully:\\n\\n1. validate output\\n2. update manifest\\n3. decide next step\\n4. launch next step immediately in the same execution flow\\n\\n**Do not stop after step success.**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5.2 Progress message rule\\nProgress messages are allowed, but only as a side effect of continued execution.\\n\\n### Valid\\n- send progress update\\n- immediately launch next command\\n- or immediately continue polling a running command\\n\\n### Invalid\\n- send progress update\\n- end turn\\n- nothing i\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L557-L633\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"citation\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L557-L633\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2285923d57b28a4ede63d1e5e1c171d55ba73cdab477c0fc561036eea2acdf07\",\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 1226,\n      \"endLine\": 1283,\n      \"score\": 1,\n      \"textScore\": 0.507416887433657,\n      \"snippet\": \"assistant: [[reply_to_current]] Absolutely — here’s a **developer checklist** for fixing the continuous-run behavior.\\n\\n# Developer Checklist — Continuous Crypto Pipeline\\n\\n## A. Workflow ownership\\n- [ ] Define the pipeline as **one active workflow**, not a series of unrelated chat replies\\n- [ ] Ensure one component clearly owns the run from **Step 0 through Step 5**\\n- [ ] Ensure Step 6 is only triggered from explicit user confirmation\\n- [ ] Prevent chat-turn boundaries from acting like implicit stop points\\n\\n---\\n\\n## B. State machine\\n- [ ] Add explicit run status values:\\n  - [ ] `idle`\\n  - [ ] `active`\\n  - [ ] `awaiting_user_confirmation`\\n  - [ ] `blocked_approval`\\n  - [ ] `blocked_error`\\n  - [\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L1226-L1283\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"citation\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L1226-L1283\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"323ca4090dd3a4e98ce45390d41d023585cda64c88319ba290c2cf3021f63075\",\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 612,\n      \"endLine\": 701,\n      \"score\": 1,\n      \"textScore\": 0.5346738909287835,\n      \"snippet\": \"- required artifact missing after retry policy exhausted\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 6) Step-by-step execution contract\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Step 0 — Initialize Run\\n\\n### Entry condition\\nUser sends:\\n- “run pipeline”\\n- “run crypto news pipeline”\\n- “start crypto pipeline”\\n\\n### Required actions\\n- generate run id and run dir\\n- create symlinks\\n- initialize manifest\\n- set:\\n  - `status=active`\\n  - `current_step=init`\\n  - `next_step=research`\\n\\n### Exit condition\\nManifest exists and init is marked succeeded.\\n\\n### Next action\\nImmediately start Step 1.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Step 1 — Research\\n\\n### Entry condition\\n- `current_step=research`\\n- `steps.research.status=pending|retrying`\\n\\n### Required actions\\n- clear researcher session file\\n- run research\\n\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L612-L701\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"citation\": \"memory/2026-05-18-bitcoin-depot.md#L612-L701\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9563a71d9395d1444332dfa3e9306780a7c3abb4cc493b380cf24bb9b3ae77d8\",\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-05-18-session-yield.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 117,\n      \"endLine\": 124,\n      \"score\": 1,\n      \"textScore\": 0.7947112490882154,\n      \"snippet\": \"If your developer intended to fix the pipeline by making the **orchestrator wait via `sessions_yield`**, that part looks good.\\n\\nIf they also intended to let me **spawn the actual worker agents directly**, then I’d want one more check after they expose those agent IDs here. Right now I only see `orchestrator`.\\n\\nIf you want, I can do one more concrete verification next:\\n- check whether `researcher`, `writer`, `creator`, and `publisher` 