{"type":"message","id":"df151e07","parentId":"649664dc","timestamp":"2026-05-21T11:25:52.833Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_EjoyhCvghf6DQrbUumZgZkSc","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[MANIFEST] step=drive status=succeeded"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":32,"aggregated":"[MANIFEST] step=drive status=succeeded","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779362752833}}
{"type":"message","id":"aef0bc99","parentId":"df151e07","timestamp":"2026-05-21T11:25:52.833Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_f2iTGbt2iDbM2ZvNJlPrDBb7","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"META\nSEO Title: Fed Master Accounts: Crypto Access Plan | Coinography\nMeta Description: The Federal Reserve opened a 60-day comment period on limited payment accounts, giving crypto and fintech firms a clearer path to core U.S. payment rails.\nURL Slug: fed-master-accounts-crypto-access-plan\nCategories: Latest News, Regulation\nPrimary Keyword: Fed master accounts\nSecondary Keywords: limited payment accounts, Fed payment rails, Ripple stablecoin\n\n# Fed master accounts open 60-day path for crypto firms\n\nThe Federal Reserve has reopened one of the most important policy debates for digital asset firms. According to [CoinDesk](https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/20/federal-reserve-proposes-limited-master-accounts-long-pursued-by-crypto-firms), the central bank started a 60-day comment period on limited payment accounts that would let eligible firms clear and settle payments through the Fed without getting full master-account status.\n\nThat matters because direct payment access can cut settlement costs and reduce dependence on partner banks. For traders, the immediate read is not a revenue jump, but a higher probability that firms tied to stablecoins, custody, and exchange settlement could gain faster dollar rails over time.\n\nThis is a policy trade, not a headline trade.\n\n## Limited payment accounts: What the Fed master accounts plan signals\n\nThe proposal gives crypto markets something they have lacked for years, a clearer framework instead of one-off fights with regional Reserve Banks. [Decrypt](https://decrypt.co/368431/trump-orders-fed-to-review-crypto-firms-access-to-master-accounts) also reported that the White House ordered the Fed to review whether non-bank financial firms can legally receive direct access to payment accounts within 120 days.\n\n\n[67 more lines in file. Use offset=21 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779362752833}}
