{"type":"message","id":"1934fe63","parentId":"9fb9c08c","timestamp":"2026-05-21T12:03:55.389Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_M6FTKHyUdPQTDKAmk1iBaIJD","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"META\nSEO Title: Fed Payment Rails Proposal Puts XRP Firms on Watch | Coinography\nMeta Description: The Fed opened a 60-day comment period on limited payment accounts, putting Ripple, Coinbase, Circle and Kraken closer to Fed payment rails.\nURL Slug: fed-payment-rails-xrp-ripple-coinbase-circle-kraken\nCategories: Regulation News, Altcoin News\nPrimary Keyword: Fed payment rails\nSecondary Keywords: limited master accounts, crypto payment rails, Ripple Fed access\n\n# Fed payment rails face a 60-day test for XRP\n\nThe Federal Reserve has opened a 60-day comment period on a limited payment-account structure that could pull selected crypto and fintech firms closer to Fed payment rails. Reports from [CoinDesk](https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/20/federal-reserve-proposes-limited-master-accounts-long-pursued-by-crypto-firms) and [CryptoSlate](https://cryptoslate.com/trump-crypto-fed-payment-rails/) show the proposal landed just after President Donald Trump ordered a review of how non-bank financial companies access Reserve Bank payment services.\n\n\n[74 more lines in file. Use offset=13 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779365035389}}
